Whoever knows God, listens to us.
In this way, we know the Spirit of truth from the spirit of error.
For love is of God.
4:8 Whoever does not love, does not know God.
4:9 The love of God was made apparent to us in this way: that God sent his only-begotten Son into the world, so that we might live through him.
4:11 Most beloved, if God has so loved us, we also ought to love one another.
But if we love one another, God abides in us, and his love is perfected in us.
4:14 And we have seen, and we testify, that the Father has sent his Son to be the Savior of the world.
4:16 And we have known and believed the love that God has for us.
For as he is, so also are we, in this world.
Instead, perfect love casts out fear, for fear pertains to punishment.
For he who does not love his brother, whom he does see, in what way can he love God, whom he does not see?
And everyone who loves God, who provides that birth, also loves him who has been born of God.
5:3 For this is the love of God: that we keep his commandments.
5:4 For all that is born of God overcomes the world.
5:5 Who is it that overcomes the world?
