While it is an ancient practice , abortion is one of the most divisive political issues of our day .
We believe it is the fact that it is a moral issue… with moral consequences that almost everyone understands to be wrong .
The Catholic Church condemns the death penalty , but the death penalty does not involve innocent human life , nor does it occur anywhere near the rate that abortions occur .
We need not describe these barbarous methods here , lest we are accused of using emotion instead of logic .
We do know , however , that approximately 50,000,000 abortions have been legally performed in the United States since the infamous Roe v .
Now , a misanthrope , who looks at people as burdens or potential burdens , may be gladdened by the fact that there are 50 million fewer people .
A life is a life whether it is in or out of the womb .
