5:6 And when I had heard their outcry in these words , I was exceedingly angry .
And I rebuked the nobles and the magistrates , and I said to them , “Have you each been exacting usury from your brothers ?
5:8 And I said to them : “As you know , in accord with what was possible for us , we have redeemed our brothers , the Jews , who had been sold to the Gentiles .
5:10 Both I and my brothers , with my servants , have lent money and grain to many .
Let us forgive the other money that is owed to us .
Then , too , the hundredth part of the money , and of the grain , wine , and oil , which you usually exact from them , give it to them.”
And we will do just as you say.” And I called the priests , and I had them swear an oath , so that they would act in accord with what I had said .
From his house and from his labors , so may he be shaken out and become empty.” And the entire multitude said , “Amen.” And they praised God .
5:14 Now from that day , on which the king had ordered me to be governor in the land of Judah , from the twentieth year even to the thirty-second year of king Artaxerxes , for twelve years , I and my brothers did not eat the yearly allowance that was owed to the governors .
And their officials also oppressed the people .
5:16 In fact , I preferred to build in the work of the wall , and I bought no land , and all my servants were gathered to do the work .
5:18 Now there was prepared for me , on each day , one ox and six choice rams , along with poultry .
Yet I did not require my yearly allowance as governor .
6:1 Now it happened that , when Sanballat , and Tobiah , and Geshem , an Arab , and our other enemies , had heard that I had built the wall , and that there was no interruption remaining in it , ( even though , at that time , I had not set up the double doors at the gates ,)
And I responded to them with the same word as before .
6:6 “It has been heard among the Gentiles , and Geshem has said it , that you and the Jews are planning to rebel , and because of this , you are building the wall and thinking to raise yourself as a king over them .
6:7 you also have stationed prophets , who preach about you in Jerusalem , saying : ‘There is a king in Judea ! ’ But the king will hear about these words .
6:8 And I sent to them , saying : “There has been nothing done according to these words , which you have spoken .
6:9 For all these men wished to frighten us , thinking that our hands would cease from the work , and that we would cease .
And let us close the doors of the temple .
I will not enter.”
6:13 For he had accepted money , so that I would be afraid , and would sin , and so that they would have some evil with which to rebuke me .
Then , too , Noadiah , a prophetess , and the rest of the prophets , would have made me afraid .
6:16 Then it happened that , when all our enemies had heard of it , all the nations that were around us were afraid , and they were downcast within themselves .
6:17 But also , in those days , many letters were being sent by the nobles of the Jews to Tobiah , and were arriving from Tobiah to them .
6:19 Moreover , they praised him before me , and they reported my words to him .
7:2 I instructed Hanani , my brother , and Hananiah , the leader of the house of Jerusalem , ( for he seemed to be a truthful man , fearing God more than the others ,)
And I stationed guards from the inhabitants of Jerusalem , each one in his turn , and each one opposite his own house .
7:5 But God had given to my heart , and I gathered the nobles , and the magistrates , and the common people , so that I might enroll them .
7:6 These are the sons of the province , who ascended from the captivity of the transmigration , those whom Nebuchadnezzar , the king of Babylon , had taken away , and who returned into Jerusalem and Judea , each one to his own city .
The number of the men of the people of Israel :
7:11 The sons of Pahath-moab of the sons of Jeshua and of Joab , two thousand eight hundred eighteen .
7:39 The priests : the sons of Jedaiah in the house of Jeshua , nine hundred seventy-three .
7:41 The sons of Pashhur , one thousand two hundred forty-seven .
7:43 The Levites : the sons of Jeshua and Kadmiel , the sons
7:46 The gatekeepers : the sons of Shallum , the sons of Ater , the sons of Talmon , the sons of Akkub , the sons of Hatita , the sons of Shobai , one hundred thirty-eight .
7:60 All the temple servants and the sons of the servants of Solomon , three hundred ninety-two .
7:64 These sought their writing in the census , and they did not find it , and so they were cast out of the priesthood .
7:66 The entire multitude , which was like one man , was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty ,
7:68 Their horses were seven hundred thirty-six ; their were mules two hundred forty-five .
7:70 Now several of the leaders of the families gave to the work .
7:71 And some of the leaders of the families gave to the treasury of the work twenty thousand drachmas of gold , and two thousand two hundred minas of silver .
7:73 Now the priests , and the Levites , and the gatekeepers , and the singing men , and the rest of the common people , and the temple servants , and all of Israel dwelt in their own cities .
8:1 And the seventh month had arrived .
And all the people were gathered together , like one man , in the street which is before the water gate .
8:2 Therefore , Ezra the priest brought the law before the multitude of men and women , and all those who were able to understand , on the first day of the seventh month .
And the ears of all the people were attentive to the book .
And standing beside him were Mattithiah , and Shemaiah , and Anaiah , and Uriah , and Hilkiah , and Maaseiah , on his right .
8:5 And Ezra opened the book before all the people .
And when he had opened it , all the people stood up .
And all the people responded , “Amen , Amen , ” lifting up their hands .
8:8 And they read from the book of the law of God , distinctly and plainly , so as to be understood .
8:9 Then Nehemiah ( the same is the cupbearer ) and Ezra , the priest and scribe , and the Levites , who were interpreting for all the people , said : “This day has been sanctified to the Lord our God .
8:10 And he said to them : “Go , eat fat foods and drink sweet drinks , and send portions to those who have not prepared for themselves .
For they understood the words that he had taught to them .
8:14 And they found written in the law , which the Lord had instructed by the hand of Moses , that the sons of Israel should live in tabernacles on the day of solemnity in the seventh month ,
8:17 Therefore , the entire assembly of those who had returned from the captivity made tabernacles and lived in tabernacles .
And they kept the solemnity for seven days .
9:2 And the offspring of the sons of Israel were separated from all the sons of foreigners .
And they adored the Lord their God .
Bless the Lord your God , from eternity even to eternity !
9:6 You yourself alone , O Lord , made heaven , and the heaven of the heavens , and all their host , the earth and all things that are in it , the seas and all things that are in them .
9:9 And you saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt .
9:10 And you gave signs and portents to Pharaoh , and to all his servants , and to the people of his land .
And you made a name for yourself , just as it is in this day .
But their pursuers you cast into the depths , like a stone into great waters .
9:13 You also descended to mount Sinai , and you spoke with them from heaven .
9:14 You revealed to them your sanctified Sabbath , and you instructed them in commandments , and ceremonies , and the law , by the hand of Moses , your servant .
And you said to them that they should enter and possess the land , over which you lifted up your hand so that you might give it to them .
9:17 And they were not willing to hear , and they did not remember , your miracles which you had accomplished for them .
But you , a forgiving God , lenient and merciful , longsuffering and full of compassion , did not abandon them .
9:19 even so , in the multitude of your mercies , you did not send them away in the desert .
9:20 And you gave them your good Spirit , so that he might teach them , and you did not withhold your manna from their mouth , and you gave them water in their thirst .
9:22 And you gave them kingdoms and peoples , and you distributed to them by lot .
9:23 And you multiplied their sons like the stars of heaven .
9:24 And the sons arrived and possessed the land .
And you delivered them into their hands , with their kings , and the people of the land , so that they might do with them just as it was pleasing to them .
And they were fattened , and they abounded with delights from your great goodness .
And they killed your prophets , who contended with them so that they might return to you .
9:27 And so you gave them into the hand of their enemies , and they afflicted them .
And you abandoned them to the hand of their enemies , and they possessed them .
Yet truly , they acted in arrogance , and they did not listen to your commandments , and they sinned against your judgments , which , if a man does them , he shall live by them .
9:30 And you continued to forbear them for many years .
And they did not listen , and so you delivered them into the hand of the peoples of the lands .
9:33 For you are just , concerning all things that have overwhelmed us .
9:34 Our kings , our leaders , our priests , and our fathers have not done your law , and they have not been attentive to your commandments and your testimonies , to which you have testified among them .
9:37 And its fruits are multiplied for the kings , whom you have set over us because of our sins .
10:31 also that , if the people of the land carry in goods for sale or any useful things , so that they might sell them on the day of the Sabbath , that we would not buy them on the Sabbath , nor on a sanctified day , and that we would release the seventh year and the collection of debt from every hand .
10:33 for the bread of the presence , and for the continual sacrifice , and for a continual holocaust on the Sabbaths , on the new moons , on the solemnities , and for the holy things , and for the sin offering , so that atonement would be made for Israel , and for every use within the house of our God .
10:35 and so that we might bring in the first-fruits of our land , and the first-fruits of all the produce from every tree , from year to year , in the house of our Lord ,
10:37 and so that we might bring in the first-fruits of our foods , and of our libations , and the fruits of every tree , also of the vintage and of the oil , to the priests , to the storehouse of our God , with the tithes of our land for the Levites .
10:38 Now the priest , the son of Aaron , shall be with the Levites in the tithes of the Levites , and the Levites shall offer a tenth part of their tithes in the house of our God , to the storeroom in the house of the treasury .
And the sanctified vessels shall be there , and the priests , and the singing men , and the gatekeepers , and the ministers .
