17:37 You have expanded my footsteps under me , and my tracks have not been weakened .
And I will not turn back until they have failed .
They will fall under my feet .
And those rising up against me , you have subdued under me .
17:44 You will rescue me from the contradictions of the people .
17:46 The sons of foreigners have been deceitful to me , the sons of foreigners have grown weak with time , and they have wavered from their paths .
17:48 O God , who vindicates me and who subdues the people under me , my liberator from my enraged enemies .
17:51 magnifying the salvation of his king , and showing mercy to David , his Christ , and to his offspring , even for all time .
18:3 Day proclaims the word to day , and night to night imparts knowledge .
18:5 Their sound has gone forth through all the earth , and their words to the ends of the world .
And his course reaches all the way to its summit .
18:8 The law of the Lord is immaculate , converting souls .
18:9 The justice of the Lord is right , rejoicing hearts .
18:10 The fear of the Lord is holy , enduring for all generations .
18:15 And the eloquence of my mouth will be so as to please , along with the meditation of my heart , in your sight , forever , O Lord , my helper and my redeemer .
May the name of the God of Jacob protect you .
19:4 May he be mindful of all your sacrifices , and may your burnt-offerings be fat .
19:6 We will rejoice in your salvation , and in the name of our God , we will be magnified .
Now I know that the Lord has saved his Christ .
The salvation of his right hand is in his power .
20:3 You have granted him the desire of his heart , and you have not cheated him of the wish of his lips .
You have placed a crown of precious stones on his head .
20:7 For you will give him as a blessing forever and ever .
20:8 Because the king hopes in the Lord , and in the mercy of the Most High , he will not be disturbed .
May your right hand discover all those who hate you .
The Lord will stir them up with his wrath , and fire will devour them .
20:12 For they have turned evils upon you ; they have devised plans , which they have not been able to accomplish .
Why have you forsaken me ?
They have spoken with the lips and shook the head .
Let him save him because he chooses him .
For tribulation is near , since there is no one who may help me .
21:14 They have opened their mouths over me , just like a lion seizing and roaring .
My heart has become like wax , melting in the midst of my chest .
And you have pulled me down , into the dust of death .
The council of the malicious has besieged me .
21:19 They divided my garments among them , and over my vestment , they cast lots .
Neither has he turned his face away from me .
21:27 The poor will eat and be satisfied , and those who yearn for the Lord will praise him .
21:28 All the ends of the earth will remember , and they will be converted to the Lord .
21:29 For the kingdom belongs to the Lord , and he will have dominion over the Gentiles .
21:32 There will be announced for the Lord a future generation , and the heavens will announce his justice to a people who will be born , whom the Lord has made .
The Lord directs me , and nothing will be lacking to me .
He has led me out to the water of refreshment .
He has led me away on the paths of justice , for the sake of his name .
For you are with me .
22:5 You have prepared a table in my sight , opposite those who trouble me .
22:6 And your mercy will follow me all the days of my life , and so may I dwell in the house of the Lord for length of days .
23:2 For he has founded it upon the seas , and he has prepared it upon the rivers .
And who will stand in his holy place ?
23:5 He will receive a blessing from the Lord , and mercy from God , his Saviour .
He himself is the King of Glory .
24:4 May all those who act unjustly over nothing be confounded .
24:6 O Lord , remember your compassion and your mercies , which are from ages past .
Remember me according to your mercy , because of your goodness , O Lord .
Because of this , he will grant a law to those who fall short in the way .
He will teach the meek his ways .
He has established a law for him , on the way that he has chosen .
24:14 The Lord is a firmament to those who fear him , and his covenant will be made manifest to them .
Deliver me from my needfulness .
24:19 Consider my enemies , for they have been multiplied , and they have hated me with an unjust hatred .
I will not be ashamed , for I have hoped in you .
25:4 I have not sat with the council of emptiness , and I will not enter with those who carry out injustice .
25:6 I will wash my hands among the innocent , and I will surround your altar , O Lord ,
25:8 O Lord , I have loved the beauty of your house and the dwelling place of your glory .
25:10 in whose hands are iniquities : their right hand has been filled by bribes .
Redeem me , and have mercy on me .
The Lord is my light and my salvation , whom shall I fear ?
26:3 If entrenched armies were to stand together against me , my heart would not fear .
26:4 One thing I have asked of the Lord , this I will seek : that I may dwell in the house of the Lord all the days of my life , so that I may behold the delight of the Lord , and may visit his temple .
In the day of evils , he has protected me in the hidden place of his tabernacle .
I have circled around and offered a sacrifice of loud exclamation in his tabernacle .
Be my helper .
26:12 Do not surrender me to the souls of those who trouble me .
My God , do not be silent toward me .
27:4 Give to them according to their works and according to the wickedness of their inventions .
Repay them with their own retribution .
27:6 Blessed is the Lord , for he has heard the voice of my supplication .
In him , my heart has hoped and I have been helped .
And from my will , I shall confess to him .
27:9 O Lord , save your people and bless your inheritance , and reign over them and exalt them , even unto eternity .
Bring to the Lord , O sons of God , bring to the Lord the sons of rams .
Bring to the Lord , glory for his name .
The Lord is over many waters .
The voice of the Lord is in magnificence .
And the Lord will quake the desert of Kadesh .
And in his temple , all will speak his glory .
And the Lord will sit as King in eternity .
The Lord will bless his people in peace .
In dedication to the house of David .
You have saved me from those who descend into the pit .
You turned your face away from me , and I became disturbed .
And I will make supplication to my God .
Will dust confess to you or announce your truth ?
The Lord has become my helper .
You have cut off my sackcloth , and you have surrounded me with joy .
O Lord , my God , I will confess to you for eternity .
In your justice , deliver me .
Hasten to rescue me .
30:4 For you are my strength and my refuge ; and for the sake of your name , you will lead me and nourish me .
For you are my protector .
But I have hoped in the Lord .
For you have looked upon my humility ; you have saved my soul from needfulness .
You have set my feet in a spacious place .
My eye has been disturbed by wrath , along with my soul and my gut .
My virtue has been weakened in poverty , and my bones have been disturbed .
Those who catch sight of me , flee away from me .
While assembled together against me in that place , they deliberated on how to take away my life .
Rescue me from the hand of my enemies and from those who are persecuting me .
Let the impious be ashamed and be drawn down into Hell .
30:20 How great is the multitude of your sweetness , O Lord , which you keep hidden for those who fear you , which you have perfected for those who hope in you , in the sight of the sons of men .
You protect them in your tabernacle , from the contradiction of tongues .
For he has shown his wonderful mercy to me , in a fortified city .
30:25 Act manfully , and let your heart be strengthened , all you who hope in the Lord .
Blessed are they whose iniquities have been forgiven and whose sins have been covered .
Yet truly , in a flood of many waters , they will not draw near to him .
You are my exultation : rescue me from those who are surrounding me .
I will fix my eyes upon you .
Their jaws are constrained with bit and bridle , so as not to draw near to you .
Exult in the Lord , you just ones ; together praise the upright .
The earth is full of the mercy of the Lord .
32:7 gathering together the waters of the sea , as if in a container , placing the depths in storage .
32:10 The Lord scatters the counsels of the nations .
32:11 But the counsel of the Lord remains for eternity , the thoughts of his heart from generation to generation .
32:14 From his well-prepared dwelling place , he has gazed upon all who dwell on the earth .
32:16 The king is not saved by great power , nor will the giant be saved by his many powers .
32:18 Behold , the eyes of the Lord are on those who fear him and on those who hope in his mercy ,
33:1 To David , when he changed his appearance in the sight of Abimelech , and so he dismissed him , and he went away .
His praise will be ever in my mouth .
May the meek listen and rejoice .
33:5 I sought the Lord , and he heeded me , and he carried me away from all my tribulations .
33:7 This poor one cried out , and the Lord heeded him , and he saved him from all his tribulations .
33:11 The rich have been needy and hungry , but those who seek the Lord will not be deprived of any good thing .
33:18 The just cried out , and the Lord heard them , and he freed them from all their tribulations .
33:20 Many are the afflictions of the just , but from them all the Lord will free them .
33:22 The death of a sinner is very harmful , and those who hate the just will fare badly .
34:2 Take hold of weapons and a shield , and rise up in assistance to me .
34:6 May their way become dark and slippery , and may the Angel of the Lord pursue them .
Over nothing , they have rebuked my soul .
34:11 Unfair witnesses have risen up , interrogating me about things of which I am ignorant .
Scourges have been gathered over me , and I was ignorant of it .
They have tested me .
Restore my soul from before their malice , my only one from before the lions .
I will praise you among a weighty people .
34:20 For indeed , they spoke peacefully to me ; and speaking with passion to the earth , they intended deceit .
Lord , do not depart from me .
34:26 Let them blush and be in awe together , those who congratulate at my misfortunes .
35:2 The unjust one has said within himself that he would commit offenses .
35:3 For he has acted deceitfully in his sight , such that his iniquity will be found to be hatred .
He is unwilling to understand , so that he may act well .
He has set himself on every way that is not good ; moreover , he has not hated evil .
35:7 Your justice is like the mountains of God .
And so the sons of men will hope under the cover of your wings .
35:12 May arrogant feet not approach me , and may the hand of the sinner not disturb me .
They have been expelled ; they were not able to stand .
Do not choose to imitate the malicious ; neither should you envy those who work iniquity .
36:3 Hope in the Lord and do good , and dwell in the land , and so you shall be pastured with its riches .
36:8 Cease from wrath and leave behind rage .
36:9 For those who are malicious will be exterminated .
36:11 But the meek shall inherit the earth , and they will delight in the multitude of peace .
36:13 But the Lord will laugh at him : for he knows in advance that his day will come .
36:15 Let their sword enter into their own hearts , and let their bow be broken .
36:17 For the arms of sinners will be crushed , but the Lord confirms the just .
Truly , the adversaries of the Lord , soon after they have been honored and exalted , will fade away , in the same way that smoke fades away .
36:22 For those who bless him will inherit the earth , but those who curse him will perish .
36:26 He shows compassion and lends , all day long , and his offspring will be in blessing .
36:28 For the Lord loves judgment , and he will not abandon his saints .
The unjust will be punished , and the offspring of the impious will perish .
36:30 The mouth of the just one will express wisdom , and his tongue will speak judgment .
When the sinners will have passed away , then you shall see .
36:37 Keep to innocence , and gaze upon fairness : because there are allotments for the peaceful man .
36:39 But the salvation of the just is from the Lord , and he is their protector in time of tribulation .
And he will rescue them from sinners and save them , because they have hoped in him .
37:4 There is no health in my flesh before the face of your wrath .
37:8 For my loins have been filled with illusions , and there is no health in my flesh .
37:12 My friends and my neighbors have drawn near and stood against me .
And those who sought my soul used violence .
And they practiced deceitfulness all day long .
And I was like someone mute , not opening his mouth .
And those who have wrongfully hated me have been multiplied .
And my substance is with you .
You have handed me over as reproach to the foolish .
Pay attention to my tears .
For I am a newcomer with you , and a sojourner , just as all my fathers were .
39:2 I have waited expectantly for the Lord , and he was attentive to me .
And he stationed my feet upon a rock , and he directed my steps .
Many will see , and they will fear ; and they will hope in the Lord .
39:6 You have accomplished your many wonders , O Lord my God , and there is no one similar to you in your thoughts .
Holocaust and sin offering , you did not require .
And your law is in the midst of my heart .
I have spoken your truth and your salvation .
39:13 For evils without number have surrounded me .
They have been multiplied beyond the hairs of my head .
39:15 Let them together be confounded and awed , who seek after my soul to steal it away .
And let those who love your salvation always say , “May the Lord be magnified.”
The Lord has been concerned about me .
The Lord will deliver him in the evil day .
And may he not hand him over to the will of his adversaries .
In his infirmity , you have changed his entire covering .
Heal my soul , because I have sinned against you.”
When will he die and his name perish ?
His heart gathered iniquity to itself .
40:9 They established an unjust word against me .
40:13 But you have sustained me , because of my innocence , and you have confirmed me in your sight in eternity .
When will I draw close and appear before the face of God ?
Meanwhile , it is said to me daily : “Where is your God ?
For I will cross into the place of the wonderful tabernacle , all the way to the house of God , with a voice of exultation and confession , the sound of feasting .
Because of this , I will remember you from the land of the Jordan and from Hermon , from the little mountain .
All your heights and your waves have passed over me .
With me is a prayer to the God of my life .
Why have you forgotten me ?
41:11 While my bones are being broken , my enemies , who trouble me , have reproached me .
Hope in God , for I will still confess to him : the salvation of my countenance and my God .
Why have you rejected me ?
Hope in God , for I will still give praise to him : the salvation of my countenance and my God .
To the sons of Korah , toward understanding .
Our fathers have announced to us the work that you wrought in their days and in the days of antiquity .
You afflicted a people , and you expelled them .
But your right hand and your arm , and the light of your countenance did so , because you were pleased with them .
43:6 With you , we will brandish a horn before our enemies ; and in your name , we will spurn those rising up against us .
43:8 For you have saved us from those who afflict us , and you have bewildered those who hate us .
43:13 You have sold your people without a price , and no great number was exchanged for them .
43:15 You have set us as a parable among the Gentiles , a shaking of the head among the peoples .
43:17 before the voice of the reproacher and the commentator , before the face of the adversary and the pursuer .
43:20 For you humbled us in a place of affliction , and the shadow of death has covered us .
For , because of you , we are being killed all day long .
My tongue is like the pen of a scribe who writes quickly .
Grace has been poured freely into your lips .
44:4 Fasten your sword to your thigh , O most powerful one .
44:6 Your arrows are sharp ; the people will fall under you , with the hearts of the enemies of the king .
The scepter of your kingdom is a scepter of true aim .
From these , they have delighted you :
The queen assisted at your right hand , in clothing of gold , encircled with diversity .
And forget your people and your father’s house .
For he is the Lord your God , and they will adore him .
44:14 All the glory of the daughter of its king is inside , in golden fringes ,
After her , virgins will be led to the king .
44:16 They will be brought with gladness and exultation .
44:18 They will remember your name always , for generation after generation .
45:3 Because of this , we will not be afraid when the earth will be turbulent and the mountains will be transferred into the heart of the sea .
45:5 The frenzy of the river rejoices the city of God .
45:7 The peoples have been disturbed , and the kingdoms have been bowed down .
45:9 Draw near and behold the works of the Lord : what portents he has set upon the earth ,
Shout joyfully to God with a voice of exultation .
46:6 God ascends with jubilation , and the Lord with the voice of the trumpet .
Sing psalms to our King , sing psalms .
Sing psalms wisely .
To the sons of Korah , on the second Sabbath .
47:3 Mount Zion is being founded with the exultation of the whole earth , on the north side , the city of the great king .
47:5 For behold , the kings of the earth have been gathered together ; they have convened as one .
47:8 With a vehement spirit , you will crush the ships of Tarshish .
God has founded it in eternity .
47:12 Let mount Zion rejoice , and let the daughters of Judah exult , because of your judgments , O Lord .
Pay attention , all inhabitants of the world :
48:4 My mouth will speak wisdom , and the meditation of my heart will speak prudence .
48:9 nor the price for the redemption of his soul .
And they will leave their riches to strangers .
They have called their names in their own lands .
And afterwards , they will delight in their mouth .
Death will feed on them .
And their help will grow old in Hell for their glory .
48:17 Do not be afraid , when a man will have been made rich , and when the glory of his house will have been multiplied .
48:19 For his soul will be blessed in his lifetime , and he will admit to you when you do good to him .
Our God also will not keep silence .
49:6 And the heavens will announce his justice .
49:10 For all the wild beasts of the forest are mine : the cattle on the hills and the oxen .
Or would I drink the blood of goats ?
49:16 But to the sinner , God has said : Why do you discourse on my justices , and take up my covenant through your mouth ?
49:18 If you saw a thief , you ran with him , and you have placed your portion with adulterers .
49:20 Sitting , you spoke against your brother , and you set up a scandal against your mother’s son .
49:22 Understand these things , you who forget God ; lest at any time , he might quickly take you away , and there would be no one to rescue you .
And in that place is the journey by which I will reveal to him the salvation of God .
A Psalm of David ,
50:4 Wash me once again from my iniquity , and cleanse me from my sin .
50:6 Against you only have I sinned , and I have done evil before your eyes .
50:7 For behold , I was conceived in iniquities , and in sinfulness did my mother conceive me .
The obscure and hidden things of your wisdom , you have manifested to me .
You will wash me , and I will be made whiter than snow .
10:32 And similarly a Levite, when he was near the place, also saw him, and he passed by.
And seeing him, he was moved by mercy.
And setting him on his pack animal, he brought him to an inn, and he took care of him.
5:1 But a certain man named Ananias, with his wife Sapphira, sold a field,
Why have you set this thing in your heart?
5:5 Then Ananias, upon hearing these words, fell down and expired.
Then the young men entered and found her dead.
5:11 And a great fear came over the entire Church and over all who heard these things.
And they all met with one accord at Solomon’s portico.
But the people magnified them.
5:19 But in the night, an Angel of the Lord opened the doors of the prison and led them out, saying,
5:21 And when they had heard this, they entered the temple at first light, and they were teaching.
And they sent to the prison to have them brought.
5:23 saying: “We found the prison certainly locked up with all diligence, and the guards standing before the door.
5:26 Then the magistrate, with the attendants, went and brought them without force.
But he was killed, and all who believed in him were scattered, and they were reduced to nothing.
For if this counsel or work is of men, it will be broken.
17:5 He created from him a helper, similar to himself.
He filled their heart with understanding, and he showed them both good and evil.
17:10 He established an eternal covenant with them, and he revealed to them his justice and judgments.
34:2 “Son of man, prophesy about the shepherds of Israel.
Should not the flocks be fed by the shepherds?
But my flock you did not feed.
What was broken, you have not bound, and what was cast aside, you have not led back again, and what was lost, you have not sought.
34:5 And my sheep were scattered, because there was no shepherd.
34:6 My sheep have wandered to every mountain and to every exalted hill.
And there was no one who sought them; there was no one, I say, who sought them.
34:10 Thus says the Lord God: Behold, I myself will be over the shepherds.
Neither will the shepherds feed themselves any more.
34:11 For thus says the Lord God: Behold, I myself will seek my sheep, and I myself will visit them.
1:2 eleven days from Horeb , by way of Mount Seir as far as Kadesh-barnea .
And so he spoke to them ,
1:6 “The Lord our God spoke to us at Horeb , saying : ‘You have remained long enough on this mountain .
For the Lord , your God , has multiplied you , and you are today like the stars of heaven , very many .
1:12 Alone , I do not have the strength to endure your arbitrations and judgments and disputes .
1:16 And I instructed them , saying : ‘Listen to them , and judge what is just , whether he is one of your citizens or a sojourner .
So you shall listen to the little as well as to the great .
But if anything seems difficult to you , then refer it to me , and I will hear it.’
1:19 Then , setting out from Horeb , we crossed through a terrible and great wasteland , which you saw along the way of the mountain of the Amorite , just as the Lord our God had instructed us .
1:20 I said to you : ‘You have arrived at the mountain of the Amorite , which the Lord our God will give to us .
Ascend and possess it , just as the Lord our God has spoken to your fathers .
1:22 And you all approached me and said : ‘Let us send men who may consider the land , and who may report as to the way by which we ought to ascend , and as to which cities we ought to travel.’
1:24 These , when they had set out and had ascended the mountains , arrived as far as the valley of the cluster of grapes .
Instead , being incredulous to the word of the Lord our God ,
And the cities are great , and the walls extend even to the sky .
1:31 And in the wilderness ( as you yourselves saw ), the Lord your God carried you , like a man who is accustomed to carrying his little son , along all the way that you walked , until you arrived at this place.’
1:33 who went before you on the way , and who marked out the place where you should pitch your tents , showing you the way by fire in the night , and by a pillar of cloud in the day .
1:35 ‘None of the men of this wicked generation will see the good land , which I have promised by oath to your fathers ,
1:38 But Joshua , the son of Nun , your minister , shall himself enter on your behalf .
1:39 Your little ones , about whom you said that they would be led away as captives , and your sons , who to this day are ignorant of the difference between good and evil , they shall enter .
1:44 And so , having gone forth , the Amorite , who was living in the mountains , came against you and pursued you , just as a swarm of bees would do .
1:45 And when you returned and were weeping in the sight of the Lord , he would not hear you , nor was he willing to agree to your voice .
And we encompassed Mount Seir for a long time .
2:3 ‘You have encompassed this mountain for long enough .
2:4 And instruct the people , saying : You shall cross through the borders of your brothers , the sons of Esau , who live at Seir , and they will fear you .
For I will not give to you from their land even as much as the step that one foot can tread upon , because I have given Mount Seir to Esau as a possession .
You shall draw water for money , and you shall drink .
The Lord your God , dwelling with you , knows your journey , how you crossed through this great wilderness over forty years , and how you have been lacking in nothing.’
2:9 And the Lord said to me : ‘You should not fight against the Moabites , nor should you go to battle against them .
2:10 The Emim were the first of its inhabitants , a people great and strong , and of such great height , like the race of the Anakim .
When these had been driven out and destroyed , the sons of Esau lived there , just as Israel did in the land of his possession , which the Lord gave to him .
2:14 Then , from the time that we advanced from Kadesh-barnea until we crossed over the torrent Zered , there were thirty-eight years , until the entire generation of the men who were fit for war had been consumed out of the camp , just as the Lord had sworn .
And giants lived there in times past , those whom the Ammonites call the Zamzummim .
2:23 Likewise the Hevites , who were living in small villages as far as Gaza , were expelled by the Cappadocians , who went forth from Cappadocia , and they wiped them out and lived in their place .
Behold , I have delivered Sihon , the king of Heshbon , the Amorite , into your hand , and so , begin to possess his land and to engage in battle against him .
We will advance by the public way .
We only ask that you allow us to pass through ,
2:32 And Sihon went out to meet us with all his people , to battle at Jahaz .
And we struck him down , with his sons and all his people .
There was not a village or city which escaped from our hands .
2:37 except the land of the sons of Ammon , which we did not approach , and all that is adjacent to the torrent Jabbok , and the cities in the mountains , and all the places which the Lord our God prohibited to us.”
And you shall do to him just as you have done to Sihon , the king of the Amorites , who lived at Heshbon.’
And we struck them down unto utter annihilation ,
There was not a village which escaped from us : sixty cities , the entire region of Argob , the kingdom of Og , in Bashan .
3:6 And we wiped them out , just as we had done to Sihon , the king of Heshbon , destroying every city , and its men , as well as women and children .
3:8 And at that time , we took the land from the hand of the two kings of the Amorites , who were across the Jordan : from the torrent Arnon as far as Mount Hermon ,
3:10 all the cities that are situated in the plain , and the entire land of Gilead and Bashan , all the way to Salecah and Edrei , cities of the kingdom of Og in Bashan .
His bed of iron is on display , ( it is in Rabbah , among the sons of Ammon ) being nine cubits in length , and four in width , according to the measure of the cubit of a man’s hand .
And I gave its cities to Ruben and Gad .
And all of Bashan is called the land of the giants .
And he called Bashan by his own name , Havvoth Jair , that is , the villages of Jair , even to the present day .
3:16 And to the tribes of Ruben and Gad , I gave from the land of Gilead as far as the torrent Arnon , one half of the torrent and its confines , even to the torrent Jabbok , which is along the border of the sons of Ammon ,
3:18 And I instructed you at that time , saying : ‘The Lord your God gives to you this land as an inheritance .
3:19 Leave behind your wives and little ones , as well as the cattle .
3:20 until the Lord provides rest to your brothers , just as he has provided for you .
So also will he do to all the kingdoms through which you shall pass .
For the Lord your God will fight on your behalf.’
3:24 ‘Lord God , you have begun to reveal your greatness and your very strong hand to your servant .
3:25 Therefore , I will cross over , and I will view this excellent land beyond the Jordan , and this singular mountain , and Lebanon.’
3:27 Ascend to the summit of Pisgah , and look around with your eyes to the west , and to the north , and to the south , and to the east , and behold it .
3:28 Instruct Joshua , and encourage and strengthen him .
3:29 And we remained in the valley , opposite the shrine of Peor.”
4:1 “And now , O Israel , listen to the precepts and judgments which I am teaching to you , so that , by doing these , you may live , and you may enter and possess the land , which the Lord , the God of your fathers , will give to you .
Preserve the commandments of the Lord your God which I am teaching to you .
4:4 But you who adhere to the Lord your God are all still alive , to the present day .
And so shall you do in the land that you will possess .
4:8 For what other nation is there so renowned as to have ceremonies , and just judgments , and the entire law that I will set forth today before your eyes ?
You should not forget the words that your eyes have seen , and do not let them be cut away from your heart , throughout all the days of your life .
4:10 from the day on which you stood before the Lord your God at Horeb , when the Lord spoke to me , saying : ‘Gather the people to me , so that they may listen to my words , and may learn to fear me , throughout all the time that they are alive on earth , and so that they may teach their children.’
And there was a darkness upon it , and a cloud , and a mist .
You heard the voice of his words , but you did not see any form at all .
4:14 And he commanded me , at that time , that I should teach you the ceremonies and judgments which you must carry out , in the land that you shall possess .
