5:1 I will sing to my beloved the canticle of my paternal cousin , about his vineyard .
5:2 And he fenced it in , and he picked the stones out of it , and he planted it with the best vines , and he built a tower in the middle of it , and he set up a winepress within it .
5:3 Now then , inhabitants of Jerusalem and men of Judah : judge between me and my vineyard .
Should I not have expected it to produce grapes , though it produced wild vines ?
I will take away its fence , and it will be plundered .
And briers and thorns will rise up .
5:7 For the vineyard of the Lord of hosts is the house of Israel .
Do you intend to live alone in the midst of the earth ?
Otherwise , many houses , great and beautiful , will become desolate , without an inhabitant .
But you do not respect the work of the Lord , nor do you consider the works of his hands .
5:14 For this reason , Hell has expanded its soul , and has opened its mouth without any limits .
5:15 And man will be bowed down , and man will be humbled , and the eyes of the exalted will be brought low .
5:17 And the lambs will pasture in proper order , and new arrivals will eat from the deserts turned into fertile lands .
5:20 Woe to you who call evil good , and good evil ; who substitute darkness for light , and light for darkness ; who exchange bitter for sweet , and sweet for bitter !
5:22 Woe to you who are powerful at drinking wine , who are strong men in contriving inebriation !
5:24 Because of this , as the tongue of fire devours stubble , and as the heat of a flame burns it completely , so will their root become like glowing embers , and so will their offshoot ascend like dust .
5:25 For this reason , the fury of the Lord has been enraged against his people , and he has extended his hand over them , and he has struck them .
5:26 And he will lift up a sign to nations far away , and he will whistle to them from the ends of the earth .
5:27 There is no one weak or struggling among them .
6:4 And the lintels above the hinges were shaken at the voice of the one crying out .
For I am a man of unclean lips , and I live in the midst of a people having unclean lips , and I have seen with my eyes the King , the Lord of hosts !
6:7 And he touched my mouth , and he said , “Behold , this has touched your lips , and so your iniquities will be taken away , and your sin will be cleansed.”
And you shall say to this people : ‘When you listen , you will hear and not understand .
6:12 For the Lord will take the men far away , and she who will have been left behind will be multiplied in the midst of the earth .
And what will remain standing within her will be a holy offspring .
7:1 And it happened in the days of Ahaz , the son of Jotham , the son of Uzziah , the king of Judah , that Rezin , the king of Syria , and Pekah , the son of Remaliah , king of Israel , ascended to Jerusalem to battle against it .
7:2 And they reported to the house of David , saying : “Syria has withdrawn to Ephraim.” And his heart was shaken , with the heart of his people , just as the trees of the forest are moved by the face of the wind .
And have no dread in your heart over the two tails of these firebrands , nearly extinguished , which are the wrath of the fury of Rezin , king of Syria , and of the son of Remaliah.”
7:6 “Let us ascend to Judah , and stir it up , and tear it away for ourselves , and appoint the son of Tabeel as a king in its midst.”
7:8 For the head of Syria is Damascus , and the head of Damascus is Rezin ; and within sixty-five years from now , Ephraim will cease to be a people .
If you will not believe , you will not continue .
7:11 Ask for a sign for yourself from the Lord your God , from the depths below , even to the heights above .
7:15 He will eat butter and honey , so that he may know to reject evil and to choose good .
7:17 The Lord will lead over you , and over your people , and over the house of your father , such days as have not occurred since the days of the separation of Ephraim from Judah by the king of the Assyrians .
7:19 And they will arrive , and they all will rest in the torrents of the valleys , and in the caverns of the rocks , and in every thicket , and in every opening .
7:24 They will enter such places with arrows and bows .
7:25 But as for all the mountains , which will be dug with a hoe , the terror of thorns and briers will not approach those places .
8:2 And I summoned to myself faithful witnesses : Uriah , the priest , and Zechariah , the son of Berechiah .
And the Lord said to me : “Call his name : ‘Rush to take away the spoils ; Hurry to be plundered.’
8:7 for this reason , behold , the Lord will lead over them the waters of a river , strong and plentiful : the king of the Assyrians with all his glory .
8:8 And he will pass through Judah , inundating it , and he will cross over and arrive , even at its neck .
Be strengthened , and be conquered !
8:12 “You should not say ‘It is conspiracy ! ’ For all that this people speaks is a conspiracy .
8:13 Sanctify the Lord of hosts himself .
8:15 And very many of them will stumble and fall , and they will be broken and entangled and seized .
8:17 And I will wait for the Lord , who has concealed his face from the house of Jacob , and I will stand before him .
8:19 And though they say to you , “Seek from seers and diviners , ” they who hiss in their incantations , should not the people seek from their God , for the sake of the living , and not from the dead ?
But if they do not speak according to this Word , then he will not have the morning light .
For he will not be able to fly away from its distress .
9:1 In the earlier time , the land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali were lifted up .
9:2 The people who walked in darkness have seen a great light .
9:3 You have increased the nation , but you have not increased the rejoicing .
9:4 For you have prevailed over the yoke of their burden , and over the rod of their shoulder , and over the scepter of their oppressor , as in the day of Midian .
And his name shall be called : wonderful Counselor , mighty God , father of the future age , Prince of Peace .
And the inhabitants of Samaria will say it , in the arrogance and haughtiness of their heart :
They have cut down the sycamores , but we will replace them with cedars.”
9:12 the Syrians from the east and the Philistines from the west .
9:16 And those who deceitfully praise this people , and those who are praised , will be thrown down violently .
And he will not take pity on their orphans and widows .
9:19 The earth has been shaken by the wrath of the Lord of hosts , and the people will become like fuel for the fire .
Each one will eat the flesh of his own arm : Manasseh Ephraim , and Ephraim Manasseh , and together they will be against Judah .
10:2 in order to oppress the poor in judgment , and to do violence to the case of the humble of my people , in order that widows may be their prey , and that they might plunder the orphan .
To whom will you flee for assistance ?
10:4 so that you may not be bowed down under the chains , and fall with the slain ?
10:6 I will send him to a deceitful nation , and I will order him against the people of my fury , so that he may take away the plunder , and tear apart the prey , and place it to be trampled like the mud of the streets .
Instead , his heart will be set to crush and to exterminate more than a few nations .
Is not Samaria like Damascus ?
10:11 Should I not do to Jerusalem and her false images , just as I have done to Samaria and her idols ? ”
10:13 For he has said : “I have acted with the strength of my own hand , and I have understood with my own wisdom , and I have removed the limits of the people , and I have plundered their leaders , and , like one with power , I have pulled down those residing on high .
And , just as the eggs which have been left behind are gathered , so have I gathered the entire earth .
10:15 Should the axe glorify itself over him who wields it ?
And he will flee away in terror .
10:20 And this shall be in that day : those not added to the remnant of Israel , and those who escape of the house of Jacob , will not lean upon him who strikes them .
10:21 The remnant of Jacob , again I say the remnant , will be converted to the mighty God .
The consummation , having been shortened , will be inundated with justice .
10:25 But after a little while and a brief time , my indignation will be consumed , and my fury will turn to their wickedness.”
10:27 And this shall be in that day : his burden will be taken away from your shoulder , and his yoke will be taken away from your neck , and the yoke will decay at the appearance of the oil .
10:29 They have passed through in haste ; Geba is our seat ; Ramah was stupefied ; Gibeah of Saul fled .
He will shake his hand against the mountain of the daughter of Zion , the hill of Jerusalem .
10:34 And the dense forest will be overturned with iron .
11:2 And the Spirit of the Lord will rest upon him : the spirit of wisdom and understanding , the spirit of counsel and fortitude , the spirit of knowledge and piety .
He will not judge according to the sight of the eyes , nor reprove according to the hearing of the ears .
And faith will be the warrior’s belt at his side .
11:7 The calf and the bear will feed together ; their young ones will rest together .
11:8 And a breastfeeding infant will play above the lair of the asp .
11:10 In that day , the root of Jesse , who stands as a sign among the people , the same the Gentiles shall beseech , and his sepulcher will be glorious .
11:12 And he will lift up a sign to the nations , and he will gather together the fugitives of Israel , and he will collect the dispersed of Judah from the four regions of the earth .
Ephraim will not be a rival to Judah , and Judah will not fight against Ephraim .
Idumea and Moab will be under the rule of their hand , and the sons of Ammon will be obedient .
Make his plans known among the peoples !
13:3 In my wrath , I commanded my sanctified ones , and I called my strong ones , those who exult in my glory .
For the Lord of hosts has given orders to soldiers of war ,
It is the Lord and the instruments of his fury , so that he may bring ruin to all the earth .
For the day of the Lord draws near !
13:7 Because of it , every hand will fail , and every heart of man will waste away and be crushed .
They will be in pain , like a woman in labor .
Their countenances will be like faces which have been burned up .
13:10 For the stars of the heavens , in their splendor , will not display their light .
13:11 And I will act against the evils of the world , and against the impious for their iniquity .
13:12 A man will be more precious than gold , and mankind will become like pure refined gold .
13:14 And they will be like a doe fleeing away , or like sheep ; and there will be no one who may gather them together .
13:15 All who are found will be killed , and all who are caught unaware will fall by the sword .
13:19 And then Babylon , the glorious one among kingdoms , that famous pride of the Chaldeans , will be destroyed , even as the Lord destroyed Sodom and Gomorrah .
The Arab will not pitch his tents there , nor will the shepherds take rest there .
13:22 And the tawny owls will answer one another there , in its buildings , and the Sirens in its shrines of pleasure .
14:1 Her time is drawing near , and her days will not be prolonged .
And the new arrival will be joined to them , and he will adhere to the house of Jacob .
14:4 you will accept this parable against the king of Babylon , and you will say : “How is it that the oppressor has ceased , along with his tribute ?
14:6 which struck the people in wrath with an incurable wound , which subjugated the nations in fury , which persecuted with cruelty .
14:8 The evergreens , too , have rejoiced over you , and the cedars of Lebanon , saying : ‘Since you have slept , no one has ascended who would cut us down.’
14:11 Your arrogance has been dragged down to Hell .
The moths will be strewn beneath you , and the worms will be your covering .
How is it that you have fallen to the earth , you who wounded the peoples ?
I will exalt my throne above the stars of God .
14:17 who made the world into a desert and destroyed its cities , who would not even open a prison for his prisoners ? ’ ”
14:19 But you have been rejected from your grave , like a useless polluted plant , and you have been bound up with those who were slain by the sword , and who descended to the bottom of the pit , like a rotting carcass .
For you have destroyed your own land ; you have slain your own people .
14:21 Prepare his sons for the slaughter , according to the iniquity of their fathers .
14:24 The Lord of hosts has sworn , saying : Surely , just as I have considered it , so shall it be , and in the same manner as I have drawn it through my mind ,
And I will cause your root to pass away by famine , and I will put to death your remnant .
For a smoke will arrive from the north , and there is no one who will escape his army .
It will be that the Lord has established Zion , and that the poor of his people will hope in him .
Because the wall of Moab has been destroyed by night , it is utterly silent .
15:3 At their crossroads , they have been wrapped with sackcloth .
15:4 Heshbon will cry out with Elealeh .
Over this , the well-equipped men of Moab wail ; each soul will wail to itself .
15:6 For the waters of Nimrim will be desolate , because the plants have withered , and the seedling has failed , and all the greenery has passed away .
15:9 Because the waters of Dibon have been filled with blood , I will place even more upon Dibon : those from Moab who flee the lion , and the survivors of the earth .
16:1 O Lord , send forth the Lamb , the Ruler of the earth , from the Rock of the desert to the mountain of the daughter of Zion .
Let your shadow be as if it were night , even at midday .
For the dust is at its end ; the miserable one has been consumed .
16:5 And a throne will be prepared in mercy , and One shall sit upon it in truth , in the tabernacle of David , judging and seeking judgment , and quickly repaying what is just .
His pride and his arrogance and his indignation is more than his strength .
Its vines have arrived even at Jazer .
Its seedlings have been abandoned .
16:9 I will weep with the tears of Jazer over this , the vineyard of Sibmah .
For the sound of those who trample has rushed over your vintage and over your harvest .
He who was accustomed to tread will not tread out the wine in the winepress .
16:11 Over this , my heart will resonate like a harp for Moab , and my inner most being for the brick wall .
16:13 This is the word that the Lord has spoken to Moab concerning that time .
Behold , Damascus will cease to be a city , and it will be like a heap of stones in ruin .
17:3 And assistance will cease from Ephraim , and the kingdom will cease from Damascus .
17:4 And this shall be in that day : the glory of Jacob will be thinned , and the fatness of his flesh will be reduced .
17:7 In that day , a man will bow before his Maker , and his eyes will consider the Holy One of Israel .
And he will not consider the things that his fingers have made , the sacred groves and the shrines .
17:11 In the day of your planting , the wild grapevine and your morning seed will flourish .
17:12 Woe to the multitude of many peoples , like the multitude of the roaring sea !
17:13 The peoples will make a noise , like the noise of waters overflowing , but he will rebuke him , and so he will flee far away .
This is the portion of those who have devastated us , and this is the lot of those who have plundered us .
18:1 Woe to the land , that winged cymbal , which is beyond the rivers of Ethiopia ,
Go forth , O swift Angels , to a nation which has been convulsed and torn apart , to a terrible people , after whom there is no other , to a nation apprehensive and downtrodden , whose land the rivers have spoiled .
18:4 For the Lord says this to me : I will be quiet , and I will consider in my place , as the light at midday is clear , and as a cloud of dew in the day of the harvest .
18:6 And together they will be abandoned to the birds of the mountains and to the wild beasts of the earth .
18:7 In that time , a gift will be carried to the Lord of hosts , from a people divided and torn apart , from a terrible people , after whom there has been no other , from an apprehensive nation , apprehensive and downtrodden , whose land the rivers have ruined , and it will be carried to the place of the name of the Lord of hosts , to mount Zion .
19:2 And I will cause Egyptian to rush against Egyptian .
19:3 And the spirit of Egypt will be ruptured to its very core .
19:5 And the waters of the sea will dry up , and the river will be desolate and dry .
The streams of its banks will diminish and dry up .
19:7 The channel of the river will be stripped down to its source , and everything irrigated by it will dry up and wither and be no more .
And all who cast a hook into the river will mourn .
19:9 Those who work with linen , combing and weaving fine textiles , will be confounded .
How can you say to Pharaoh : “I am the son of wisemen , the son of the kings of antiquity ?
Let them announce it to you , and let them reveal what the Lord of hosts intends for Egypt .
19:14 The Lord has mixed a spirit of giddiness into its midst .
19:15 And there will be no work for Egypt that would produce a head or a tail , one who bows down or one who refrains from bowing down .
19:18 In that day , there will be five cities in the land of Egypt which speak the language of Canaan , and which swear by the Lord of hosts .
19:19 In that day , there will be an altar of the Lord in the midst of the land of Egypt and a monument of the Lord beside its borders .
And they will make vows to the Lord , and they will fulfill them .
And they will return to the Lord .
19:23 In that day , there will be a way from Egypt to the Assyrians , and the Assyrian will enter into Egypt , and the Egyptian will be with the Assyrians , and the Egyptians will serve Assur .
19:25 which the Lord of hosts has blessed , saying : Blessed be my people of Egypt , and the work of my hands for the Assyrian , but Israel is my inheritance .
20:1 In the year in which Tharthan entered into Ashdod , when Sargon , the king of the Assyrians , had sent him , and when he had fought against Ashdod and had captured it ,
20:3 And the Lord said : Just as my servant Isaiah has walked naked and barefoot , as a sign and as a portent of three years over Egypt and over Ethiopia ,
20:5 And they will be afraid and confounded over Ethiopia , their hope , and Egypt , their glory .
And now , how will we be able to escape ?
21:2 A difficult vision has been announced to me : he who is unbelieving , he acts unfaithfully , and he who is a plunderer , he devastates .
21:3 Because of this , my lower back has been filled with pain , and anguish has possessed me , like the anguish of a woman in labor .
I was disturbed when I saw it .
21:8 And a lion cried out : “I am on the watchtower of the Lord , standing continually by day .
